{"id":"45a6cfd7-dd37-4a60-8c22-8d7928ade45b","object":"chat.completion","created":1784984082,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"import heapq\\nfrom collections import defaultdict\\n\\ndef solve(case):\\n    nodes = case.get('nodes')\\n    req_symbols = case.get('required_symbols')\\n    if not nodes or not req_symbols:\\n        raise ValueError('Missing nodes or required_symbols')\\n    \\n    node_map = {}\\n    children = defaultdict(list)\\n    symbol_count = defaultdict(int)\\n    \\n    for n in nodes:\\n        nid = n.get('id')\\n        parent = n.get('parent')\\n        symbol = n.get('symbol')\\n        depth = n.get('depth')\\n        removable = n.get('removable')\\n        utility = n.get('utility')\\n        if nid is None or parent is None or symbol is None or depth is None or removable is None or utility is None:\\n            raise ValueError('Node missing required field')\\n        node_map[nid] = {'id': nid, 'parent': parent, 'symbol': symbol, 'depth': depth, 'removable': removable}\\n        if parent is not None:\\n            children[parent].append(nid)\\n        symbol_count[symbol] += 1\\n    \\n    # Validate required symbols exist\\n    for sym in req_symbols:\\n        if symbol_count.get(sym, 0) == 0:\\n            raise ValueError(f'Required symbol {sym} not present')\\n    \\n    retained = set(node_map.keys())\\n    removal_order = []\\n    \\n    # Initial leaf candidates: removable, not root, no children\\n    heap = []\\n    for nid, nd in node_map.items():\\n        if nd['removable'] and nid != 'root' and len(children.get(nid, [])) == 0:\\n            heapq.heappush(heap, (-nd['depth'], nid))\\n    \\n    while heap:\\n        neg_depth, nid = heapq.heappop(heap)\\n        if nid not in retained:\\n            continue\\n        nd = node_map[nid]\\n        # Check leaf condition: no retained children\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children.get(nid, [])):\\n            continue\\n        # Check root and removable\\n        if nid == 'root' or not nd['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        # Check required symbol preservation\\n        if nd['symbol'] in req_symbols and symbol_count[nd['symbol']] == 1:\\n            continue\\n        # Remove node\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        symbol_count[nd['symbol']] -= 1\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n        # Parent might become leaf\\n        parent = nd['parent']\\n        if parent is not None and parent in retained:\\n            pnode = node_map[parent]\\n            if all(c not in retained for c in children.get(parent, [])):\\n                if pnode['removable'] and parent != 'root':\\n                    heapq.heappush(heap, (-pnode['depth'], parent))\\n    \\n    retained_ids = sorted(retained)\\n    return {\\n        'retained_ids': retained_ids,\\n        'removal_order': removal_order\\n    }\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to parse the task. It's about \"grammar_guided_node_reduction\" on a parse tree. The payload has nodes with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility. Also required_symbols list. The goal is to reduce the tree by removing nodes that are removable, but must preserve that all required_symbols are still represented in the tree after removal. Also cannot remove the root (id \"root\"?) or nodes that have retained children (i.e., if you remove a node, you must remove its descendants? The description says \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" That implies we can only remove leaf nodes? Actually read more: \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" And \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\" \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" \"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\"\n\nWe need to output a result: probably retained node IDs sorted, and removal order list.\n\nThe problem: we have a tree of nodes. Some nodes are removable (removable=True). We want to remove some removable nodes while preserving that all symbols in required_symbols are present in the set of retained nodes. Also we cannot remove a node that has any retained children (i.e., if a node is removed, all its descendants must also be removed? Or the node must be leaf? Actually \"Never remove ... a node with retained children.\" Means if a node has children that are retained, we cannot remove it. So we can only remove leaf nodes? But leaf nodes might have children? No, leaf has no children. So we can only remove leaves that are removable. But also we must consider that removing a node might affect ancestors: if we remove a leaf, its parent might become leaf and then could be removed if it's removable and still preserves required symbols. So we need a process: start from deepest nodes? The instruction: \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\" That suggests a post-order traversal. For each node (starting from deepest), if it is removable, and if removing it does not cause any required symbol to be lost (i.e., the symbol of that node is not required, or if there are other nodes with that symbol? Actually required_symbols is a list of symbols that must be present in the entire tree after removal. So if we remove a node, we need to ensure that the symbol it provides is still present elsewhere. Also we cannot remove if it has any retained children. So we traverse nodes in decreasing depth. For each node, if removable, and all its children are already removed (so it's a leaf in the current retained set), and if removing it still leaves all required symbols represented (i.e., after removal, for each required symbol, there is at least one node with that symbol that is retained), then we can remove it. We also need to consider that removing a node might affect ancestors' leaf status. So we should do this iteratively: after each removal, the parent may become